          "title": "You'll want to know: 意想不到",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "意想不到 — yìxiǎngbúdào — \"unexpected; beyond what anyone imagined\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "这真是一个意想不到的好方法 zhè zhēn shì yí ge yìxiǎngbúdào de hǎo fāngfǎ — That really is an unexpectedly good way of doing it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "不 is said with a rising tone before the falling tone of dào: bú dào."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "意想不到 (yìxiǎngbúdào) is built from 意 'the mind', 想 'to think', 不 'not' and 到 'to reach', all inherited from Middle Chinese, 'iH, sjangX, pjut and tawH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription): what the mind's thinking does not reach."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
